applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIHARA, TOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIHARA TOSHINOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIHARA, TOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A composition for biodegradable plastic molding which comprises (A) 100 parts by weight of a biodegradable plastic component consisting mainly of an aliphatic polyester and (B) preferably 5 to 55 parts by weight of a biodegradable component consisting mainly of a starchy material comprising a modified starch. The composition can be subjected to secondary processings such as cutting and bonding and can be molded into a biodegradable sheet having a desired rigidity.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à une composition pour le moulage de plastique biodégradable, qui comprend: (A) 100 parties en poids d'un constituant en plastique biodégradable composé essentiellement d'un polyester aliphatique; et (B) de préférence 5 à 55 parties en poids d'un constituant biodégradable composé essentiellement d'une matière amidée renfermant un amidon modifié. Cette composition peut être soumise à des traitements secondaires, tels que des opérations de coupe et de liaison, et elle peut être moulée en une feuille biodégradable ayant la rigidité souhaitée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms